.TH cbspkg 1 2026-11-09 "sandogasa 0.27.1" "Sandogasa Manual"
.SH NAME
cbspkg \- Package and build for CentOS SIGs in CBS, the way fedpkg does for Fedora
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcbspkg\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Package and build for CentOS SIGs in CBS, the way fedpkg does for Fedora
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH COMMANDS
.SS cbspkg config
\fBcbspkg config\fR [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.PP
Set up the GitLab token
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Ask for every setting again, with the saved value as the default: Enter keeps it, a new value replaces it, and \- clears an optional one
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS cbspkg sig-repo
\fBcbspkg sig\-repo\fR [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-explain\fR] [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-sig\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIMR_URL|PACKAGE\fR>
.PP
Make sure the SIG has its repo for a package, a pull mirror of CentOS Stream\*(Aqs, and push a merge request\*(Aqs change to it
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show each step without doing anything
.TP
\fB\-\-explain\fR
Narrate each step and show its command, pausing before each
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
The dist\-git checkout to push from (default: the current directory)
.TP
\fB\-\-sig\fR \fI<SIG>\fR
The SIG, for a package name (a merge request is always a Proposed Update)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
hyperscale
.IP \(bu 2
proposed\-updates
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Create the repo without asking
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIMR_URL|PACKAGE\fR>
A CentOS Stream merge request URL (a Proposed Update), or a package name
